Umbra: libvlcjni without renderer discovery (RendererDiscoverer.java is GPL).

libvlc/src/org/videolan/libvlc/RendererDiscoverer.java carries a GPL-2.0-or-later
header (every other Java/Kotlin file of libvlcjni at 965e8648 is LGPL-2.1-or-later
or has no header; the library is published as LGPL 2.1, libvlc/COPYING.LIB).
Umbra never casts and never looks for renderers, so the class is left out of the
AAR instead (docs/COMPLIANCE.md §1.4). scripts/build-libvlc-android.sh deletes
RendererDiscoverer.java and its JNI side, libvlc/jni/libvlcjni-rendererdiscoverer.c
(LGPL, used by nothing else), before anything is built; this patch removes what
referred to them:
  * JNI_OnLoad no longer looks up org/videolan/libvlc/RendererDiscoverer and its
    Description (FindClass would fail without the class, and libvlcjni.so would
    not load), nor their two static factory methods, and no longer frees them;
  * libvlcjni-rendererdiscoverer.c is no longer compiled (Android.mk);
  * the RendererDiscoverer field block goes from utils.h.
RendererItem.java stays (LGPL by COPYING.LIB: MediaPlayer.setRenderer and
util/DisplayManager use the type), but nothing can create one any more: its
constructor is package-private and RendererDiscoverer was its only caller, so
its native release method (which lived in the removed C file) is never reached.
MediaPlayer.setRenderer(null) still works.

diff --git a/libvlc/jni/Android.mk b/libvlc/jni/Android.mk
index a165816..32e37be 100644
--- a/libvlc/jni/Android.mk
+++ b/libvlc/jni/Android.mk
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ LOCAL_MODULE    := libvlcjni
 LOCAL_SRC_FILES := libvlcjni.c
 LOCAL_SRC_FILES += libvlcjni-mediaplayer.c
 LOCAL_SRC_FILES += libvlcjni-vlcobject.c
-LOCAL_SRC_FILES += libvlcjni-media.c libvlcjni-medialist.c libvlcjni-mediadiscoverer.c libvlcjni-rendererdiscoverer.c
+LOCAL_SRC_FILES += libvlcjni-media.c libvlcjni-medialist.c libvlcjni-mediadiscoverer.c
 LOCAL_SRC_FILES += libvlcjni-dialog.c
 LOCAL_SRC_FILES += std_logger.c
 LOCAL_C_INCLUDES := $(VLC_SRC_DIR)/include $(VLC_BUILD_DIR)/include
